{"agent":"fx-init-folds","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"When the handshake detects that another process appended events between `_load(repo, agent)` and `log.read_all()`, it reassigns the local variable `st` to a newly folded state, but it does not update the `_SCOPE` cache entry set by `_load`. A later `_load(repo, agent)` in the same `load_scope` still receives the original cached `(log, cfg, st)` with the old `event_count`. For example, if the log has N events when `_load` caches state N, another process appends one before the handshake's `read_all` returns N+1, the handshake reports values computed from N+1 events while a following `_upgrade_line`/plan reader gets state N from the cache. This makes the handshake and the instructions see different moments, directly contradicting the branch's own “the upgrade line reads the same state” comment.","digest":"b63cde906ad48841","location":"ddflow/api/surf_mcp.py:223","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/surf_mcp.py:223"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":7788,"diff_sha":"24e5f702037c680c95cb416a7bb4e8920e2572b861f45ccc1d6fdfd4bfdaa033","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":1,"files":2,"insertions":22,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":498.7,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"ed62587560812cd8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-mcp-initialize-folds-log.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T174342Z-60057471.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"50b097eba9aa798c30a8d90be755d589c070107f","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/_base.py":"100644 e23a107609bdb59d3bdd0e1527e75e610f8eceba","ddflow/api/surf_mcp.py":"100644 a0f9118aa41224035265bfd6ea0a31c1c31454be","ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py":"100644 11e5b31aceb7d6d7e66b9a328411dc50